<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ALLOWLIST, not a denylist. The previous version included ALL of `sharedpref` and excluded a
  single filename, so any prefs file added later was backed up by default — which is how a
  plaintext credential file became eligible for Google Drive backup.

  With an <include> present, the ruleset is SCOPED to it: anything not named here is already
  excluded. Do NOT add <exclude> elements — a path outside the included scope is a FATAL
  FullBackupContent lint error ("… is not in an included path") that fails lintVitalRelease and
  blocks the release build entirely, while debug builds and the whole unit suite stay green.

  The security properties below therefore hold by OMISSION, deliberately:
    - secure_store.xml (Keystore-wrapped credentials) — not listed, never backed up
    - domain="file"     (the 190 MB whisper model, the 325 MB Kokoro voice, and any future
                         session-audio archive) — not listed, never backed up
    - domain="database" — not listed, never backed up

  NEVER restore `<include domain="sharedpref" path="."/>`. That is the denylist form that made a
  plaintext API key eligible for Drive backup and device-to-device transfer.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <include domain="sharedpref" path="whisper_everywhere_prefs.xml" />
</full-backup-content>
